From 4b37ac6a2d8550adb396c95f880923db233f39b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Samson <valentin_samson@nps-bea.fr>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:02:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Sunshine port: menu rendering, pixel metrics, copy
 read-back, viewport offset

- Viewport origin decoded and encoded with the SDK's 342 offset (was 340):
  everything the game drew was 2 pixels off, which made Delfino's
  pollution layers drift every frame through their EFB copy loop.
- Pixel metrics: GX_LOAD_AURORA_PIXEL_METRIC makes the following draws
  count the fragments that pass the alpha test into a counter slot, read
  back asynchronously per frame (aurora/sms_ext.h, gfx/sms_readback).
- EFB copy read-back for the game's RAM copy of a texture.
- Data copies (intensity, channels, depth) at the game's resolution with
  nearest sampling.
- PartyBoard menu rendering, live graphics settings and retained frames
  (by Codex).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
