From c2402ef8f045473e6826e9eec51c9c0aaf287e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin SAMSON <BEAVSN@BEA.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:39:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Sunshine port: data passes, display copies, EFB peeks,
 depth copies, pipeline cache, frame generation support

Changes that the sms-unified bridge has been using from the working tree,
committed together so the patch series builds what the bridge calls.

From the port's Aurora work (Codex sessions):
- end_frame(present) and finish_recording_frame: a frame can be recorded
  without being presented.
- begin_data_pass/end_data_pass: native-resolution offscreen passes for the
  pollution data copies; copy_display/select_scanout: XFB copies and the
  scanout the VI chooses (black when it says so).
- peek_efb (efb_peek.cpp), copy_depth_efb and the asynchronous depth copies
  (Corona's bathtub depth on the CPU).
- Copy read-back requests with ids, rejected requests, a capacity check and
  a checkpoint that submits sealed copies; read-back slots.
- Pipeline cache: SQLite corruption handling, precompilation before gameplay,
  pipelines that must be complete for EFB texture draws; profiling switches.

For frame generation (SMS_FRAMEGEN in the port):
- aurora_sms_present_after: the next presented frame waits until then; the
  render worker keeps the present pending (defer_present) and goes on with
  the next frame's passes, pumping Dawn's events meanwhile, and is not idle
  while a present is pending.
- aurora_sms_set_frames_in_flight: 2 frames in flight by default, 3 on
  request (staging buffers follow); AURORA_PRESENT_LOG=<n> logs the time
  between presents.

